{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1740,1846p' .task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n## 17. Validation and independent-review checks\n\nRequired packet validation:\n\n- every fenced JSON example parses, including the exact init/fetch/SSH and\n  `cat-file --batch` arrays;\n- unsubstituted source omits `substitution`;\n- substituted source requires both `substituted: true` and a typed substitution;\n- mixed marker v3 carries receipt v1 for local `go-v1`, receipt v2 for external commands, and top-level skill build-source only because a local build is active;\n- all revision-1 findings remain mapped to sections 3, 5, 6, 8, and 9;\n- all revision-2 findings map to exact network argv (6.2–6.3), SSH\n  isolation (6.4), and local format/ref/object admission (6.5–6.6);\n- all revision-3 findings map to the single raw-object process and byte\n  protocol (6.1, 6.6.1), pack 2/3 plus index-2 local admission (6.5.3), and the\n  all-blob LFS detector (6.6.3);\n- all revision-4 findings map to the pinned parser-family detector and\n  cross-language LFS fixtures (6.6.3), plus the common commit/tag byte grammar,\n  semantic result, and network/local parity fixtures (6.6.2);\n- no project/spec/code/schema/test/release/prior-resource file changes.\n\nIndependent review should decide:\n\n1. Is the declared/effective receipt shape sufficient to prevent substitution/cache confusion?\n2. Do the exact init/fetch vectors prevent remote/package/default selection of\n   local refs, helper, refspec, tags, submodules, maintenance, `FETCH_HEAD`,\n   filter, server option, or upload-pack?\n3. Does the fixed SSH wrapper admit only the tested protocol-v0 destination and\n   remote command, and does the OpenSSH vector suppress user/system config,\n   prompts, TTY, forwarding, proxy/jump/local-command/control behavior while\n   retaining only the required private Git protocol pipe?\n4. Does local v1 fail stably for gitfile/linked/bare/reftable/unknown layouts\n   and unambiguously parse ordinary config, files refs, loose objects, and\n   exact pack/index pairs without running source Git behavior?\n5. Does the single full-OID `cat-file --batch` contract close request,\n   response, transformation, child-process, network, missing-object, and\n   resource-limit behavior for both network and inert-copied local stores?\n6. Are pack versions 2/3 and index version 2 defined identically for SHA-1 and\n   SHA-256 managers, with all other physical formats rejected stably?\n7. Does the pinned Git LFS 3.7.1-family detector cover every accepted\n   key/value and encoder form, including extension suffixes, duplicate\n   behavior, signed/zero-padded sizes, exact cutoff, endings/order, and\n   non-empty size zero, while keeping a closed ordinary-blob boundary?\n8. Does the common commit/tag byte grammar accept signed and extra-header\n   objects while rejecting duplicate/misordered structural headers, malformed\n   separators, wrong target types, cycles, and depth overflow with the same\n   semantic result on both source paths?\n9. Are URL, SSH trust, tag, and structured development-ref rules exact enough for cross-language implementations?\n10. Are whole-snapshot audit and pre-cache ordering coherent on real, cache-hit, and dry-run paths?\n11. Can marker v3 represent local-only, external-only, and mixed installations without changing receipt-v1/schema-6 meaning?\n12. Do status, repair, deduplication, rollback, and GC fail closed without executing source or built output?\n13. Does logical target selection satisfy repository target selection while preserving manager-derived binary names and paths?\n14. Are signing and future-driver boundaries still closed?\n\n### 17.1 Producer verification evidence\n\nChecks performed on 2026-07-27:\n\n- all twelve fenced JSON documents parsed with the host Python JSON parser;\n- targeted topic checks found the exact init/fetch vectors,\n  `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`, wrapper argv contract, `-F` SSH isolation, stable\n  gitfile/bare/linked/reftable errors, config/ref grammar, exact pack-2/3 and\n  index-2 admission, the full-OID-only batch request/response grammar, manager\n  object-ID recomputation, common commit/tag semantic grammar, pinned-family\n  all-blob LFS detector, audit-before-cache/compiler ordering, mixed\n  receipt/marker behavior, status/repair/GC, signing, future-driver rules, and\n  board-impact mapping;\n- the new Git fetch/init/repository-version/reftable/layout/config and OpenSSH\n  manual pages in section 16 were opened from their primary maintainers and\n  checked against the claims above;\n- a temporary local-transport smoke on Git 2.50.1 exercised the exact\n  init/common-fetch option shape for both full-object and exact-tag refspecs,\n  verified the fixed `refs/curator/*` destinations, and verified that\n  `FETCH_HEAD` was absent;\n- a task-local Git 2.50.1 raw-object smoke used the exact `cat-file --batch`\n  argv against SHA-1 and SHA-256 private repositories; full-ID requests\n  returned the documented `<oid> <type> <size> LF`, exact content bytes, and\n  terminal LF, while no filter/textconv/mailmap option or child process was\n  used;\n- Git LFS 3.7.1 source and binary checks confirmed the `<1024` cutoff,\n  `bytes.TrimSpace`/ScanLines behavior, current/alias versions, one-digit\n  prefix-only extension regexp, exact-key overwrite, distinct-priority\n  rejection, signed-int64 size parsing, and empty encoding for size zero;\n- the checked official `v3.7.1/lfs/pointer.go` bytes hashed to\n  `sha256:3aa4a0df7ed9b3c8f45742a4e01909feeb721017bfbd70e2a166132b2a814b2d`;\n  the local binaries were Git 2.50.1 and Git LFS 3.7.1;\n- pinned Git LFS 3.7.1 strict checks returned zero for the canonical lowercase,\n  dot/dash, underscore, uppercase, and punctuation-suffix extension fixture,\n  and returned two for the deliberately noncanonical non-empty size-zero\n  fixture;\n- independent cross-language fixture checks covered the exact 1023/1024 cutoff,\n  CRLF/blank/unsorted/no-final-LF forms, exact duplicate keys, distinct\n  duplicate priorities, non-empty size zero, punctuation-start and uppercase-\n  OID near misses;\n- Git 2.50.1 raw-object smoke and the manager grammar fixtures covered valid\n  signed/extra-header commits and tags, duplicate/misordered tree/object/type\n  headers, malformed separators, declared/actual target mismatch, and identical\n  network-private/local-inert expected results;\n- unchanged curator-spec validation passed:\n  `validated 30 schemas and 93 vector files`;\n- the pinned validation environment's full `make validate` passed all 30\n  schemas, 93 vectors, 8 Python tests, and `go test ./tools/...`;\n- all five newly relied-on pinned Git LFS/Git data-model/signature URLs\n  returned HTTP 200;\n- `git diff --check` passed in curator-spec;\n- this run did not edit product/spec/schema/code/test/release files or either\n  prior producer/reviewer resource.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
