{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba .task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md | sed -n '330,520p'\"","aggregated_output":"   330\tGIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=1\n   331\tGIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM=1\n   332\tGIT_EXEC_PATH=<fingerprinted trusted Git exec path>\n   333\tHOME=<operation-private>/home\n   334\tXDG_CONFIG_HOME=<operation-private>/config\n   335\tLC_ALL=C\n   336\tLANG=C\n   337\t```\n   338\t\n   339\tFor SSH it additionally sets only\n   340\t`GIT_SSH=<absolute-manager-wrapper>`, `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`, and the\n   341\tmanager-private policy-FD number. `GIT_PROTOCOL` is absent and the fixed\n   342\tconfiguration uses protocol version 0, so Git MUST NOT add an SSH\n   343\t`SendEnv=GIT_PROTOCOL` option. For HTTPS, `GIT_ASKPASS` names either the\n   344\tmanager credential broker or a fail-closed manager broker.\n   345\t\n   346\tThe manager unsets `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_WORK_TREE`, `GIT_COMMON_DIR`,\n   347\t`GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY`, `GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES`, `GIT_NAMESPACE`,\n   348\t`GIT_REPLACE_REF_BASE`, `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE`, `GIT_SSL_NO_VERIFY`,\n   349\t`GIT_SSH_COMMAND`, `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `SSH_ASKPASS`, `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`,\n   350\t`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_*`, `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_*`, all trace variables, all HTTP/HTTPS\n   351\tproxy variables, and every other inherited `GIT_*`/`SSH_*` variable. `PATH` is\n   352\ta manager-owned empty directory except for exact helper basenames that the\n   353\tfingerprinted Git family cannot launch by absolute exec-path resolution.\n   354\t\n   355\tHTTPS verifies TLS and does not follow redirects. An operator proxy or\n   356\tcredential may be supplied only through manager policy/broker state, never the\n   357\tmanifest, descriptor, source repository, or compiler environment.\n   358\t\n   359\t### 6.2 Exact private repository initialization\n   360\t\n   361\tBefore each network attempt the manager exclusively creates a new empty\n   362\toperation-private directory, an actual zero-entry template directory, empty\n   363\thooks directory, and private bare-repository path. It invokes exactly:\n   364\t\n   365\t```json\n   366\t[\n   367\t  \"<absolute-trusted-git>\",\n   368\t  \"--git-dir=<operation-private>/repo.git\",\n   369\t  \"-c\",\n   370\t  \"init.defaultBranch=curator-invalid\",\n   371\t  \"init\",\n   372\t  \"--bare\",\n   373\t  \"--quiet\",\n   374\t  \"--template=<operation-private>/empty-template\",\n   375\t  \"--object-format=<sha1-or-sha256>\",\n   376\t  \"--ref-format=files\"\n   377\t]\n   378\t```\n   379\t\n   380\tThere is no repository path operand, global/user/system template, initial\n   381\tbranch from configuration, shared mode, separate Git directory, worktree, or\n   382\tsource-provided config. After exit, manager code opens the result with\n   383\tno-follow/rooted access and requires:\n   384\t\n   385\t- one ordinary bare repository inside operation-private state;\n   386\t- `core.repositoryformatversion`/`extensions.objectFormat` consistent with the\n   387\t  requested object format and files refs;\n   388\t- no remote, alternate, promisor, partial-clone, worktree, replace, graft,\n   389\t  shallow, hook, filter, or unknown extension state;\n   390\t- no link, reparse escape, special file, unexpected owner/ACL, or writable\n   391\t  boundary outside the operation principal.\n   392\t\n   393\tFailure discards the directory. The manager never repairs or adopts it.\n   394\t\n   395\t### 6.3 Exact network fetch and ref flows\n   396\t\n   397\tAll fetches use a direct validated URL, a fresh private repository, one\n   398\tmanager-chosen destination under `refs/curator/`, and this exact common shape:\n   399\t\n   400\t```json\n   401\t[\n   402\t  \"<absolute-trusted-git>\",\n   403\t  \"--git-dir=<operation-private>/repo.git\",\n   404\t  \"--no-replace-objects\",\n   405\t  \"--no-lazy-fetch\",\n   406\t  \"--no-optional-locks\",\n   407\t  \"-c\",\n   408\t  \"protocol.allow=never\",\n   409\t  \"-c\",\n   410\t  \"protocol.<https-or-ssh>.allow=always\",\n   411\t  \"-c\",\n   412\t  \"protocol.version=0\",\n   413\t  \"-c\",\n   414\t  \"credential.helper=\",\n   415\t  \"-c\",\n   416\t  \"core.askPass=<manager-broker>\",\n   417\t  \"-c\",\n   418\t  \"core.hooksPath=<operation-private>/empty-hooks\",\n   419\t  \"-c\",\n   420\t  \"core.fsmonitor=false\",\n   421\t  \"-c\",\n   422\t  \"core.untrackedCache=false\",\n   423\t  \"-c\",\n   424\t  \"submodule.recurse=false\",\n   425\t  \"-c\",\n   426\t  \"fetch.recurseSubmodules=false\",\n   427\t  \"-c\",\n   428\t  \"maintenance.auto=false\",\n   429\t  \"-c\",\n   430\t  \"fetch.writeCommitGraph=false\",\n   431\t  \"-c\",\n   432\t  \"fetch.fsckObjects=true\",\n   433\t  \"-c\",\n   434\t  \"transfer.fsckObjects=true\",\n   435\t  \"-c\",\n   436\t  \"http.followRedirects=false\",\n   437\t  \"-c\",\n   438\t  \"http.sslVerify=true\",\n   439\t  \"-c\",\n   440\t  \"http.proxy=\",\n   441\t  \"-c\",\n   442\t  \"https.proxy=\",\n   443\t  \"fetch\",\n   444\t  \"--quiet\",\n   445\t  \"--atomic\",\n   446\t  \"--no-tags\",\n   447\t  \"--no-recurse-submodules\",\n   448\t  \"--no-auto-maintenance\",\n   449\t  \"--no-write-fetch-head\",\n   450\t  \"--no-write-commit-graph\",\n   451\t  \"--refmap=\",\n   452\t  \"--jobs=1\",\n   453\t  \"--upload-pack=git-upload-pack\",\n   454\t  \"--\",\n   455\t  \"<validated-url>\",\n   456\t  \"<one-manager-refspec>\"\n   457\t]\n   458\t```\n   459\t\n   460\tThe selected transport is the only `protocol.*.allow=always` entry; the other\n   461\ttransport and every remote-helper protocol remain denied. There is no\n   462\t`--filter`, `--server-option`, remote name, configured refspec, stdin refspec,\n   463\tprune, mirror, depth/shallow option, tag auto-follow, or package-selected\n   464\targument. Top-level `git fetch` receives closed stdin and bounded captured\n   465\tdiagnostics.\n   466\t\n   467\tThe one refspec is selected as follows:\n   468\t\n   469\t1. **Declared lock, primary attempt:**  \n   470\t   `<full-locked-oid>:refs/curator/locked`. A full hexadecimal object name is\n   471\t   the only non-ref source admitted. On success, the manager still parses and\n   472\t   recomputes that object and requires a commit.\n   473\t2. **Declared lock, exact-tag fallback:**  \n   474\t   If and only if the primary attempt fails and the declaration contains a\n   475\t   validated tag, discard the entire failed repository, initialize a new one,\n   476\t   and fetch\n   477\t   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/tag`. Manager code parses the resulting direct\n   478\t   ref and any annotated-tag chain, recomputes every tag object, peels to a\n   479\t   commit, and requires exact equality with the locked object ID. Mismatch is\n   480\t   `build_repository_ref_moved`. There is no branch/all-tags fallback.\n   481\t3. **Operator network substitution:**  \n   482\t   A full `revision` fetches\n   483\t   `<full-oid>:refs/curator/effective`; a `tag` fetches\n   484\t   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/effective`; a `branch` fetches\n   485\t   `refs/heads/<branch>:refs/curator/effective`. There is no fallback between\n   486\t   forms. The declared repository lock's object format initializes the private\n   487\t   repository and MUST match the substituted remote; the manager never retries\n   488\t   under another hash family. The exact resulting commit becomes the effective\n   489\t   receipt identity.\n   490\t\n   491\tEvery destination is fixed manager namespace text; remote data cannot choose a\n   492\tlocal ref, refmap, refspec, helper, upload-pack, filter, or server option.\n   493\t`FETCH_HEAD`, remote-tracking refs, local heads/tags, commit-graphs, and\n   494\tmaintenance state MUST remain absent. A nonzero fetch, unexpected local ref,\n   495\tunexpected child, or any write outside the private repository fails and\n   496\tdiscards the attempt.\n   497\t\n   498\t### 6.4 Exact SSH wrapper and OpenSSH invocation\n   499\t\n   500\tSSH sources retain the section-3 canonical identity but are further narrowed\n   501\tfor this driver: the raw repository path supplied to the remote shell MUST use\n   502\tonly ASCII letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `-`, and `/`, with the existing\n   503\tnon-empty/no-`.`/no-`..` component rules. A quote, shell metacharacter,\n   504\twhitespace, escape, or non-ASCII byte is therefore rejected for SSH before\n   505\tGit. HTTPS retains the section-3 path grammar.\n   506\t\n   507\tBefore fetch, the manager creates a protected read-only policy record and\n   508\tpasses an already-open descriptor number to the binary wrapper. The record\n   509\tcontains exactly:\n   510\t\n   511\t- the expected Git destination, either `host` or `user@host`;\n   512\t- the expected raw remote path from the validated SSH URI/SCP spelling;\n   513\t- the expected remote command\n   514\t  `git-upload-pack '<raw-path>'`;\n   515\t- absolute operator-trusted SSH executable, empty SSH config, empty global\n   516\t  known-hosts file, selected operator known-hosts file, timeout, and exactly\n   517\t  one authentication mode.\n   518\t\n   519\tBecause the allowed path alphabet excludes `'`, the command has no escaping\n   520\tbranch. The wrapper does not accept a policy pathname from argv/environment and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
