{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba .temp/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md | sed -n '1704,1818p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1704\t\n  1705\t### 13.3 Required controls\n  1706\t\n  1707\t| Threat | Control |\n  1708\t|---|---|\n  1709\t| Mutable/symbolic revision | Full object-format commit lock; optional safe tag must peel exactly |\n  1710\t| Declared/effective substitution confusion | Both states and substitution type in receipt-v2 input/cache key |\n  1711\t| Replace refs or grafts | Reject refs/grafts and use `--no-replace-objects` |\n  1712\t| Partial clone or lazy fetch | Reject promisor state and use `--no-lazy-fetch`; prove all tree/blob objects local |\n  1713\t| Alternates/object-store escape | Reject alternate files/env and manager-copy into private object DB |\n  1714\t| Fetch default widens state/process graph | Exact fresh-repo init/fetch argv; fixed destination ref; no tags, submodules, `FETCH_HEAD`, maintenance, commit graph, refmap, filter, or server option |\n  1715\t| Ambient config/URL rewrite/proxy/helper | Empty global/system config, manager-owned repo, fixed config/env/process graph |\n  1716\t| SSH MITM, system config, or variant argv | `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`; exact wrapper shape; `-F` empty config; operator-known hosts; fixed OpenSSH argv |\n  1717\t| Local repository extension/ref ambiguity | Admit only ordinary files-ref layout; byte-level config/ref parser; reject gitfile, commondir, bare, reftable, or unknown extensions |\n  1718\t| Malicious/incomplete pack metadata | Pack v2/v3 plus index-v2 admission, hash-family filenames/trailers, inert private copying, fixed trusted `cat-file --batch`, and manager object-ID recomputation |\n  1719\t| Object-reader transformation or process escape | One full-OID-only batch grammar; no `ls-tree`, revision/path input, filter, textconv, mailmap, alternate, lazy fetch, or object-reader child |\n  1720\t| Commit/tag parser disagreement | One ordered manager byte grammar, reserved-header uniqueness, exact separator, actual target-type checks, and one stable semantic error on both source paths |\n  1721\t| Hook/filter/LFS/submodule execution | Raw object extraction; no checkout/archive transforms; pinned Git LFS 3.7.1-family conservative all-blob detector; reject gitlinks |\n  1722\t| Package output/argv/signing selection | Strict descriptor; command-key output; closed driver; no signing fields |\n  1723\t| Audit bypass on cache hit | Exact snapshot validation/hash/audit before artifact-cache lookup |\n  1724\t| Forged cache | Protected boundary plus exact digests; rebuild rather than adopt |\n  1725\t| Shim/PATH hijack | Structural no-follow/hash validation; manager-generated shims; never execute output |\n  1726\t| Partial/cross-project install | One manager-home journaled transaction; consumer last; reverse rollback |\n  1727\t\n  1728\tSame-principal/admin compromise remains outside the local protected-cache invariant. Receipt and marker hashes are consistency/currentness identifiers, not signatures.\n  1729\t\n  1730\t## 14. Exact impact on existing board work\n  1731\t\n  1732\tThis scope is a new schema-7/rc.5 delivery subtree. It MUST NOT reopen, relabel, or silently expand rc.4 work.\n  1733\t\n  1734\t### 14.1 Existing curator-spec schema-6 story\n  1735\t\n  1736\t`STORY-260720-35dck7` (“Protocol schema v6”) and all 12 child tasks remain rc.4 evidence. In particular:\n  1737\t\n  1738\t- `TASK-260720-1nvomm`, `TASK-260720-17llva`, and `TASK-260720-wajgn8` remain the schema-6 core/profile/manifest contract;\n  1739\t- `TASK-260720-12iigs`, `TASK-260720-2zc6k1`, and `TASK-260720-37ei85` remain receipt-v1/marker-v2, claim-v2, and legacy guards;\n  1740\t- `TASK-260720-1s1vr6`, `TASK-260720-cw39jh`, `TASK-260720-1u7hes`, `TASK-260720-3lo9jc`, `TASK-260720-q5oy3o`, and `TASK-260720-3ag6pi` remain rc.4 vectors, gates, docs, release metadata, and integrated verification.\n  1741\t\n  1742\tNo existing schema-6 task should absorb schema 7. After architecture acceptance, the smallest new curator-spec set is:\n  1743\t\n  1744\t1. core/security/decision contract;\n  1745\t2. wire schemas and generated schema cases;\n  1746\t3. manager profile/CLI including Git, substitutions, status/repair/GC;\n  1747\t4. conformance/release gates including raw-object, mixed-build, and claim-v3 vectors.\n  1748\t\n  1749\tTask-local tests/docs stay with those deliverables; no ceremonial extra task is justified.\n  1750\t\n  1751\t### 14.2 Existing Curator implementation story\n  1752\t\n  1753\t`STORY-260720-3plyvy` (“Curator Go build driver”) remains the local schema-6 `go-v1` implementation. Its manifest, source identity, toolchain, receipt/cache, marker, shim, transaction, lifecycle, docs, and rc.4 verification tasks are prerequisites/reusable foundations, not owners of external Git semantics.\n  1754\t\n  1755\tA later external-repository Curator story consumes those foundations and adds:\n  1756\t\n  1757\t- schema-7/repository/descriptor/substitution models;\n  1758\t- clean Git acquisition and raw-object snapshot admission;\n  1759\t- independent external audit subjects;\n  1760\t- receipt v2, marker v3, mixed-command planning, snapshot-cache currentness/GC;\n  1761\t- end-to-end rc.5 vectors.\n  1762\t\n  1763\tDo not change `TASK-260720-1zntv0` or other `go-v1` tasks to accept Git fields or arbitrary build behavior.\n  1764\t\n  1765\t### 14.3 Existing cocoaskills implementation story\n  1766\t\n  1767\t`STORY-260720-1uv5gi` (“csk Go build driver”) likewise remains the independent local schema-6 implementation. A new external-repository story should build on its schema model, transaction engine, source/toolchain identities, protected caches, planner, currentness/repair/GC, docs, and E2E gates.\n  1768\t\n  1769\tThe new work owns Python-specific clean Git/raw-object handling, external audit subjects, receipt-v2/marker-v3 mixed builds, substitutions, and rc.5 vectors. Existing `git archive` behavior is not sufficient unless independently proven byte-identical and free of attributes/filters; the recommended implementation is raw object extraction.\n  1770\t\n  1771\t### 14.4 Existing interoperability story\n  1772\t\n  1773\t`STORY-260720-21bsr2` (“Compiled-build interoperability”) remains rc.4/schema-6 evidence. Its 12 tasks, including shared compiled cases, native consumers, black-box runner, authoring guide, language-driver gate, release qualification, and pins, MUST NOT claim schema 7.\n  1774\t\n  1775\tAfter both managers implement schema 7, a downstream rc.5 interoperability extension adds exact cross-language comparisons for:\n  1776\t\n  1777\t- canonical URL/ref parsing and SHA-1/SHA-256 locks;\n  1778\t- raw snapshot bytes/digest and declared/effective identities;\n  1779\t- unsubstituted/substituted/mixed receipt and marker bytes;\n  1780\t- unavailable, moved, alternate/replace/graft/promisor, helper/filter/LFS/submodule negatives;\n  1781\t- cache hit/miss/corruption, status/repair/GC, shim/PATH, rollback, and release evidence.\n  1782\t\n  1783\tLinux remains a separate later native-validation item and cannot be listed in claim v3 until it passes.\n  1784\t\n  1785\t## 15. Rejected alternatives\n  1786\t\n  1787\t- Add Git/ref/output fields to a build command: duplicates source declarations and reopens output control.\n  1788\t- Let the descriptor name a binary/output: violates manager-derived output and collision/path safety.\n  1789\t- Reuse `go-v1`: changes source acquisition, identity, receipt, and marker meaning under an rc.4 driver.\n  1790\t- Tag-only, branch, abbreviated ID, or raw revision grammar: mutable or ambiguous compiler input.\n  1791\t- Trust a source or artifact cache without exact protected admission and audit: bypasses source policy.\n  1792\t- Permit replacements, alternates, grafts, partial clones, lazy fetch, local upload-pack, submodules, or LFS: adds unbound objects, processes, credentials, or network.\n  1793\t- Use `git clone`, an implicit/default fetch, or a named remote: admits template/config/refspec/tag/submodule/maintenance behavior not selected by the manager.\n  1794\t- Inherit Git/SSH/proxy/helper/filter configuration: transfers process/network control outside the closed manager policy.\n  1795\t- Auto-detect the SSH variant or pass the source SSH configuration: permits variant-dependent argv and system/user proxy, command, identity, forwarding, or control behavior.\n  1796\t- Admit gitfiles, linked worktrees, bare repositories, reftable, unknown repository extensions, optional pack sidecars, pack versions outside 2/3, or pack indexes outside v2 in local-substitution v1: requires additional containment/parser semantics and vectors; reject with stable errors instead.\n  1797\t- Let each manager choose its own documented pack/index subset: makes the same local substitution non-interoperable; v1 fixes pack 2/3 plus index 2.\n  1798\t- Use `ls-tree`, `--batch-command`, pretty-printers, revision/path expressions, checkout, archive, filters, textconv, or mailmap for extraction: adds redundant grammars or repository-selected transformations; one full-OID `cat-file --batch` stream is sufficient.\n  1799\t- Let `cat-file` type labels choose among malformed commit/tag headers: local raw objects can contain duplicate or misordered structural headers; the manager applies one exact semantic grammar after recomputing IDs.\n  1800\t- Treat recognized Git LFS pointer text as compiler source: a package can make a pointer visible through `go:embed` while the actual bytes remain outside the locked Git graph; v1 rejects every form accepted by the pinned Git LFS 3.7.1 parser family before audit.\n  1801\t- Store only effective substitution state: loses declared provenance; store only declared state: misdescribes compiled bytes.\n  1802\t- Upgrade every schema-7 command to receipt v2: unnecessarily changes local `go-v1`; mixed explicit versions preserve rc.4 semantics.\n  1803\t- Install-time signing/notarization: introduces secrets, post-processing children, mutable services, and new identity not covered by the first driver.\n  1804\t- Standardize physical cache/checkouts: machine-local layout remains implementation-specific.\n  1805\t\n  1806\t## 16. Primary-source register\n  1807\t\n  1808\tChecked on 2026-07-27:\n  1809\t\n  1810\t- Git global options and environment isolation, including `--no-replace-objects`, `--no-lazy-fetch`, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`, `GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM`, `GIT_SSH`, and prompt controls: https://git-scm.com/docs/git\n  1811\t- Exact fetch defaults and controls, including tag auto-follow, `FETCH_HEAD`, auto-maintenance, commit-graph writing, refmap, submodule recursion, upload-pack, filters, and full-object refspecs: https://git-scm.com/docs/git-fetch\n  1812\t- Private repository initialization, object format, files/reftable ref format, and template selection: https://git-scm.com/docs/git-init\n  1813\t- Repository format version and mandatory extension recognition/rejection: https://git-scm.com/docs/repository-version\n  1814\t- Reftable repository extension, stack, and dummy files that make implicit files-ref parsing unsafe: https://git-scm.com/docs/reftable\n  1815\t- Repository layout, gitfiles, commondir/linked worktrees, loose/packed refs, shallow, graft, alternate, and object-pack state: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitrepository-layout\n  1816\t- Pack and index structure/checksum surfaces, including pack versions 2/3,\n  1817\t  index version 2, SHA-1/SHA-256 widths, fanout/offset tables, and trailers:\n  1818\t  https://git-scm.com/docs/gitformat-pack\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
