checks\n  1862\t\n  1863\tRequired packet validation:\n  1864\t\n  1865\t- every fenced JSON example parses, including the exact init/fetch/SSH and\n  1866\t  `cat-file --batch` arrays;\n  1867\t- unsubstituted source omits `substitution`;\n  1868\t- substituted source requires both `substituted: true` and a typed substitution;\n  1869\t- mixed marker v3 carries receipt v1 for local `go-v1`, receipt v2 for external commands, and top-level skill build-source only because a local build is active;\n  1870\t- all revision-1 findings remain mapped to sections 3, 5, 6, 8, and 9;\n  1871\t- all revision-2 findings map to exact network argv (6.2–6.3), SSH\n  1872\t  isolation (6.4), and local format/ref/object admission (6.5–6.6);\n  1873\t- all revision-3 findings map to the single raw-object process and byte\n  1874\t  protocol (6.1, 6.6.1), pack 2/3 plus index-2 local admission (6.5.3), and the\n  1875\t  all-blob LFS detector (6.6.3);\n  1876\t- all revision-4 findings map to the pinned parser-family detector and\n  1877\t  cross-language LFS fixtures (6.6.3), plus the common commit/tag byte grammar,\n  1878\t  semantic result, and network/local parity fixtures (6.6.2);\n  1879\t- no project/spec/code/schema/test/release/prior-resource file changes.\n  1880\t\n  1881\tIndependent review should decide:\n  1882\t\n  1883\t1. Is the declared/effective receipt shape sufficient to prevent substitution/cache confusion?\n  1884\t2. Do the exact init/fetch vectors prevent remote/package/default selection of\n  1885\t   local refs, helper, refspec, tags, submodules, maintenance, `FETCH_HEAD`,\n  1886\t   filter, server option, or upload-pack?\n  1887\t3. Does the fixed SSH wrapper admit only the tested protocol-v0 destination and\n  1888\t   remote command, and does the OpenSSH vector suppress user/system config,\n  1889\t   prompts, TTY, forwarding, proxy/jump/local-command/control behavior while\n  1890\t   retaining only the required private Git protocol pipe?\n  1891\t4. Does local v1 fail stably for gitfile/linked/bare/reftable/unknown layouts\n  1892\t   and unambiguously parse ordinary config, files refs, loose objects, and\n  1893\t   exact pack/index pairs without running source Git behavior?\n  1894\t5. Does the single full-OID `cat-file --batch` contract close request,\n  1895\t   response, transformation, child-process, network, missing-object, and\n  1896\t   resource-limit behavior for both network and inert-copied local stores?\n  1897\t6. Are pack versions 2/3 and index version 2 defined identically for SHA-1 and\n  1898\t   SHA-256 managers, with all other physical formats rejected stably?\n  1899\t7. Does the pinned Git LFS 3.7.1-family detector cover every accepted\n  1900\t   key/value and encoder form, including extension suffixes, duplicate\n  1901\t   behavior, signed/zero-padded sizes, exact cutoff, endings/order, and\n  1902\t   non-empty size zero, while keeping a closed ordinary-blob boundary?\n  1903\t8. Does the common commit/tag byte grammar accept signed and extra-header\n  1904\t   objects while rejecting duplicate/misordered structural headers, malformed\n  1905\t   separators, wrong target types, cycles, and depth overflow with the same\n  1906\t   semantic result on both source paths?\n  1907\t9. Are URL, SSH trust, tag, and structured development-ref rules exact enough for cross-language implementations?\n  1908\t10. Are whole-snapshot audit and pre-cache ordering coherent on real, cache-hit, and dry-run paths?\n  1909\t11. Can marker v3 represent local-only, external-only, and mixed installations without changing receipt-v1/schema-6 meaning?\n  1910\t12. Do status, repair, deduplication, rollback, and GC fail closed without executing source or built output?\n  1911\t13. Does logical target selection satisfy repository target selection while preserving manager-derived binary names and paths?\n  1912\t14. Are signing and future-driver boundaries still closed?\n  1913\t\n  1914\t### 17.1 Producer verification evidence\n  1915\t\n  1916\tChecks performed on 2026-07-27:\n  1917\t\n  1918\t- all twelve fenced JSON documents parsed with the host Python JSON parser;\n  1919\t- targeted topic checks found the exact init/fetch vectors,\n  1920\t  `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`, wrapper argv contract, `-F` SSH isolation, stable\n  1921\t  gitfile/bare/linked/reftable errors, config/ref grammar, exact pack-2/3 and\n  1922\t  index-2 admission, the full-OID-only batch request/response grammar, manager\n  1923\t  object-ID recomputation, common commit/tag semantic grammar, pinned-family\n  1924\t  all-blob LFS detector, audit-before-cache/compiler ordering, mixed\n  1925\t  receipt/marker behavior, status/repair/GC, signing, future-driver rules, and\n  1926\t  board-impact mapping;\n  1927\t- the new Git fetch/init/repository-version/reftable/layout/config and OpenSSH\n  1928\t  manual pages in section 16 were opened from their primary maintainers and\n  1929\t  checked against the claims above;\n  1930\t- a temporary local-transport smoke on Git 2.50.1 exercised the exact\n  1931\t  init/common-fetch option shape for both full-object and exact-tag refspecs,\n  1932\t  verified the fixed `refs/curator/*` destinations, and verified that\n  1933\t  `FETCH_HEAD` was absent;\n  1934\t- a task-local Git 2.50.1 raw-object smoke used the exact `cat-file --batch`\n  1935\t  argv against SHA-1 and SHA-256 private repositories; full-ID requests\n  1936\t  returned the documented `<oid> <type> <size> LF`, exact content bytes, and\n  1937\t  terminal LF, while no filter/textconv/mailmap option or child process was\n  1938\t  used;\n  1939\t- Git LFS 3.7.1 source and binary checks confirmed the `<1024` cutoff,\n  1940\t  `bytes.TrimSpace`/ScanLines behavior, current/alias versions, one-digit\n  1941\t  prefix-only extension regexp, exact-key overwrite, distinct-priority\n  1942\t  rejection, signed-int64 size parsing, and empty encoding for size zero;\n  1943\t- the checked official `v3.7.1/lfs/poin