{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff --no-index --unified=2 -- .task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md .temp/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md b/.temp/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md\nindex 7e2c0de..175c669 100644\n--- a/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md\n+++ b/.temp/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n-# External build repositories: architecture decision and threat model, revision 5\n+# External build repositories: architecture decision and threat model, revision 6\n \n **Task:** `TASK-260720-1nvomm`  \n **Date:** 2026-07-27  \n **Status:** Superseding architecture proposal for independent review  \n-**Supersedes:** `TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v4.md`  \n-**Review input:** `TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-review-v4.md`  \n+**Supersedes:** `TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md`  \n+**Review input:** `TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-review-v5.md`  \n **Scope:** Architecture only. No protocol, schema, manager, test, CLI, release, or prior decision artifact was changed.\n \n@@ -34,29 +34,22 @@ shim name              = <manifest-command-key>\n An external source is first-class compiler input. Before an artifact-cache lookup or compiler child, the manager MUST resolve or load the exact effective Git commit, freeze its complete regular-file snapshot, validate and hash it, and audit it as a separate subject from the consuming skill. This ordering applies to real operations, cache hits, and dry-runs that claim source verification.\n \n-### 1.1 Changes required by the fourth independent review\n-\n-This revision preserves every accepted revision-4 section and closes its final\n-two bounded interoperability findings:\n-\n-1. The LFS invariant is now explicitly tied to the pinned and tested Git LFS\n-   3.7.1 pointer parser/encoder family. The all-blob detector is a bounded\n-   conservative byte parser that covers every pointer form accepted by that\n-   family, including extension names beginning with `_`, uppercase ASCII, and\n-   punctuation-bearing suffixes; exact 1024-byte cutoff; leading/trailing\n-   whitespace, blank-line, LF/CRLF, ordering, duplicate-key/priority, signed and\n-   zero-padded size behavior; and the deliberately noncanonical non-empty\n-   `size 0` form. It still has a closed false-positive boundary and never\n-   invokes `git-lfs`.\n-2. Commit and annotated-tag bytes now have one manager-owned grammar on both\n-   network and local paths. It fixes required header order and uniqueness,\n-   full object-ID width/case, parent ordering, metadata and continuation\n-   handling, exact LF separator rules, bounded ignored messages, tag-chain\n-   cycle/depth rules, and actual target-type matching. Every malformed\n-   commit/tag semantic input fails one stable pre-audit error before tree\n-   materialization or audit.\n-\n-The prior exact Git process/object/pack controls, source identity,\n-receipt/marker/cache behavior, audit ordering, status/repair/GC, output,\n-signing, future-driver, and board-impact decisions are unchanged.\n+### 1.1 Change required by the fifth independent review\n+\n+This revision preserves every accepted revision-5 section and closes its one\n+bounded tag-verification finding:\n+\n+1. An unsubstituted declaration containing `tag` now always uses one fresh\n+   exact-tag fetch as both acquisition and verification. It never tries the\n+   full locked object ID first. Manager code recomputes and peels the fetched\n+   lightweight or annotated tag chain and requires the terminal commit to\n+   equal `locked_commit.hex` before audit success, artifact-cache lookup, or a\n+   compiler child. A moved tag is `build_repository_ref_moved`; an absent or\n+   inaccessible exact tag is `build_repository_source_unavailable`. Direct\n+   full-object fetch remains available only for declarations without `tag`.\n+\n+The prior LFS detector, common commit/tag grammar, exact Git process/object/pack\n+controls, source identity, receipt/marker/cache behavior, audit ordering,\n+status/repair/GC, output, signing, future-driver, and board-impact decisions\n+are unchanged.\n \n ### 1.2 Justified gap and self-verification\n@@ -172,7 +165,16 @@ The full object ID is the immutable lock. The tag is only a human-facing asserti\n 1. The effective declared-source repository object format MUST equal `locked_commit.object_format`.\n 2. The object named by `locked_commit.hex` MUST exist and be a commit.\n-3. If `tag` is present, its tag ref MUST peel to that exact commit under `--no-replace-objects`; mismatch is `build_repository_ref_moved`.\n+3. If `tag` is present on an unsubstituted declaration, the manager MUST\n+   acquire exactly `refs/tags/<tag>` in fresh operation-private state, recompute\n+   and peel its lightweight or annotated tag chain under\n+   `--no-replace-objects`, and require the terminal commit to equal\n+   `locked_commit.hex`. Mismatch is `build_repository_ref_moved`; a missing or\n+   inaccessible exact ref is `build_repository_source_unavailable`.\n 4. Install, repair, status, and audit never rewrite a lock. An authoring command may propose a manifest change, but it is outside installation.\n-5. A server that does not permit fetching an unadvertised locked object may require the optional tag to retrieve it. Failure to obtain the exact locked commit is an availability error, never permission to widen the fetch or accept another commit.\n+5. A declaration without `tag` acquires only the full locked object ID. A\n+   declaration with `tag` acquires only the exact tag ref; server permission to\n+   fetch a direct object ID is irrelevant and MUST NOT change this choice.\n+   Failure never permits a branch, all-tags, alternate-ref, or direct-object\n+   fallback.\n \n ## 4. Repository descriptor and output boundary\n@@ -467,16 +469,23 @@ diagnostics.\n The one refspec is selected as follows:\n \n-1. **Declared lock, primary attempt:**  \n-   `<full-locked-oid>:refs/curator/locked`. A full hexadecimal object name is\n-   the only non-ref source admitted. On success, the manager still parses and\n-   recomputes that object and requires a commit.\n-2. **Declared lock, exact-tag fallback:**  \n-   If and only if the primary attempt fails and the declaration contains a\n-   validated tag, discard the entire failed repository, initialize a new one,\n-   and fetch\n-   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/tag`. Manager code parses the resulting direct\n-   ref and any annotated-tag chain, recomputes every tag object, peels to a\n-   commit, and requires exact equality with the locked object ID. Mismatch is\n-   `build_repository_ref_moved`. There is no branch/all-tags fallback.\n+1. **Unsubstituted declaration without `tag`:**  \n+   Fetch `<full-locked-oid>:refs/curator/locked`. A full hexadecimal object\n+   name is the only non-ref source admitted. On success, manager code still\n+   parses and recomputes that object and requires a commit. A nonzero fetch is\n+   `build_repository_source_unavailable`. There is no tag, branch, advertised\n+   ref, or all-refs fallback.\n+2. **Unsubstituted declaration with `tag`:**  \n+   Always fetch\n+   `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/curator/tag` as the sole acquisition attempt. The\n+   manager MUST NOT first or later fetch `<full-locked-oid>`, even when the\n+   server permits direct object-ID wants. Manager code requires exactly the\n+   fixed destination ref, parses and recomputes a lightweight or annotated-tag\n+   chain with section 6.6.2's common grammar, and requires the terminal object\n+   to be a commit exactly equal to `locked_commit.hex`. A different terminal\n+   commit is `build_repository_ref_moved`. A missing exact ref, nonzero fetch,\n+   or transport failure is `build_repository_source_unavailable`. A malformed\n+   or incomplete fetched object graph retains the section 6.6 stable semantic\n+   or incomplete-source error. There is no direct-object, branch, all-tags, or\n+   alternate-ref fallback.\n 3. **Operator network substitution:**  \n    A full `revision` fetches\n@@ -496,4 +505,85 @@ unexpected child, or any write outside the private repository fails and\n discards the attempt.\n \n+For an unsubstituted tagged source, exact-tag fetch and terminal-lock equality\n+are preconditions of source resolution. They run before source audit can\n+succeed, before artifact-cache lookup, and before any compiler child. A failure\n+publishes no snapshot, audit success, receipt, marker, or artifact. A\n+syntax-only offline check that cannot perform the exact-tag fetch emits only\n+`build_repository_unverified_offline`; install, update, repair, and\n+coverage-claiming audit return `build_repository_source_unavailable` before\n+mutation.\n+\n+The conformance matrix is invariant to direct object-ID want policy because a\n+tagged declaration never issues such a want:\n+\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"tag-match-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n+    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n+    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n+    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n+    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n+    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n+    \"result\": \"source-resolved\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"tag-moved-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n+    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n+    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n+    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n+    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n+    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n+    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_ref_moved\",\n+    \"audit_started\": false,\n+    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n+    \"compiler_started\": false\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"tag-missing-direct-oid-wants-denied\",\n+    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"deny\",\n+    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n+    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n+    \"remote_ref_present\": false,\n+    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_source_unavailable\",\n+    \"audit_started\": false,\n+    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n+    \"compiler_started\": false\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"tag-match-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n+    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n+    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n+    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n+    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n+    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n+    \"result\": \"source-resolved\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"tag-moved-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n+    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n+    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n+    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n+    \"tag_terminal_commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n+    \"locked_commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n+    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_ref_moved\",\n+    \"audit_started\": false,\n+    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n+    \"compiler_started\": false\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"tag-missing-direct-oid-wants-permitted\",\n+    \"server_direct_oid_wants\": \"permit\",\n+    \"fetch_refspec\": \"refs/tags/v1.4.0:refs/curator/tag\",\n+    \"direct_oid_fetch_attempted\": false,\n+    \"remote_ref_present\": false,\n+    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_source_unavailable\",\n+    \"audit_started\": false,\n+    \"artifact_cache_lookup\": false,\n+    \"compiler_started\": false\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n ### 6.4 Exact SSH wrapper and OpenSSH invocation\n \n@@ -1250,10 +1340,12 @@ The consuming skill snapshot and each effective external repository snapshot are\n For every external repository selected by the active plan:\n \n-1. validate the whole repository snapshot;\n-2. compute `curator-build-source-v1` over every regular file, including `curator-build.json` and files outside the selected build root;\n-3. parse the descriptor and select the target;\n-4. audit the complete external snapshot under declared/effective identity, object format, effective commit, build-source digest, target, and substitution state;\n-5. apply allowlist, revocation, registry, tag-lock, and audit policy gates;\n-6. only then inspect an artifact-cache candidate or start a compiler child.\n+1. for an unsubstituted declaration containing `tag`, complete the exact-tag\n+   acquisition and terminal-lock equality check from section 6.3;\n+2. validate the whole repository snapshot;\n+3. compute `curator-build-source-v1` over every regular file, including `curator-build.json` and files outside the selected build root;\n+4. parse the descriptor and select the target;\n+5. audit the complete external snapshot under declared/effective identity, object format, effective commit, build-source digest, target, substitution state, and the verified tag assertion when applicable;\n+6. apply allowlist, revocation, registry, tag-lock, and audit policy gates;\n+7. only then inspect an artifact-cache candidate or start a compiler child.\n \n Registry evidence for the skill does not attest the external repository. External evidence does not attest the skill. Audit cache reuse is allowed only when its subject tuple exactly matches the declared/effective state and snapshot digest; it does not bypass snapshot admission.\n@@ -1387,4 +1479,13 @@ The complete receipt-v2 input is canonicalized with CCJ-1. Its SHA-256 is the ar\n Receipt v2 retains exact canonical stored bytes, manager-derived artifact path, artifact SHA-256, and byte size. It has no trust/provenance boolean. Protected-state admission remains out of band.\n \n+For `effective.substituted: false`, the presence of `declared.tag` is a semantic\n+receipt precondition: the writer may emit and publish the receipt only after\n+that operation's exact-tag acquisition proves the tag terminates at\n+`declared.locked_commit`. A self-asserted `tag_verified` boolean is not added;\n+it would not prove the fetch. Receipt admission instead depends on the fixed\n+operation ordering and protected snapshot/receipt boundary. A substituted\n+receipt records the manifest's declared tag only as declared state and makes no\n+claim that the remote tag was consulted while compiling substituted bytes.\n+\n ### 8.3 Mixed command behavior\n \n@@ -1458,4 +1559,9 @@ Illustrative mixed marker excerpt:\n ```\n \n+For an unsubstituted external build, `declared_tag` may be written only from a\n+receipt whose producing operation completed the exact-tag/locked-commit check.\n+Marker parsing does not turn that field into independent provenance, and\n+read-only status does not contact the remote to re-test later tag movement.\n+\n ### 9.1 Snapshot and artifact keys\n \n@@ -1490,4 +1596,9 @@ Outcomes:\n Repair resolves the current effective operator substitution if present, otherwise the declared locked source. It reacquires into operation-private state, repeats object proof, validation, identity, and audit, and rebuilds or reuses only after protected admission. It never adopts an untrusted snapshot or artifact by changing permissions.\n \n+For an unsubstituted declaration containing `tag`, repair always reacquires by\n+the exact-tag-only flow and rechecks terminal equality with the immutable lock.\n+It cannot use a successful direct-object fetch or an old protected snapshot